What:		/sys/kernel/q2_suspend/s2idle
KernelVersion:	7.3
Description:
		Allows suspend-to-idle on the Ingenic X2000 when the kernel
		is built with CONFIG_INGENIC_X2000_NORMAL_SLEEP. Reading
		returns 0 or 1. Writing a boolean accepted by kstrtobool()
		sets it; the write takes the system sleep lock, so it does not
		change the setting during a transition. The default is 0.

		While it is 0, writing "freeze" to /sys/power/state, or
		"s2idle" to /sys/power/mem_sleep followed by "mem" to
		/sys/power/state, fails with -EINVAL before devices are
		suspended. While it is 1, suspend-to-idle runs through the
		generic PM core, which owns device suspend and wake
		interrupts; the platform's retained-memory deep sleep is
		not used for it.

		The file is mode 0600.
